<doc node='1280922e-00f5' rev='3'><paragraph id='mmgx2r82dhj.0' rev='1' h='fe9ecb57' heading='1'><text id='.1'>PP-001: New repository tooling should default to Python</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.56' h='f11c3f34' heading='2'><text id='.57'>Thesis</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.63' h='26e9bc8c'><text id='.64'><bold>Thesis</bold></text><text id='.70'>: New command-line tooling in a repository that already uses Python should be written in Python, not Node.js, unless a script needs a Node.js library with no equivalent.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.239' h='2f73e880' heading='2'><text id='.240'>Audience and Stakes</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.259' rev='2' h='0b5e7f85'><text id='.260'>Maintainers choosing a runtime for a new tooling script. A second runtime in a repository adds installation and </text><text id='.1724'>maintenance</text><text id='.378'> for every contributor.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.401' rev='1' h='481da3a7' heading='2'><text id='.402'>Argument</text></paragraph><list id='.410' h='57f98ef6' kind='ordered'><listItem id='.411' h='5e0f03ef'><paragraph id='.412' h='55effba1'><text id='.413'>Both runtimes handle text and file work comparably on the cited assessment. [TA-001, Comparison]</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.509' h='1802429d'><paragraph id='.510' h='0a875b72'><text id='.511'>A repository with one runtime has less to install and maintain than one with two. Author's judgment.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.611' h='74ac3639'><paragraph id='.612' h='b89dbd35'><text id='.613'>So the existing runtime wins unless a library requires the other. Author's judgment.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.697' h='41ff72e0' heading='2'><text id='.698'>Objections and Answers</text></paragraph><table id='.720' rev='3' h='1541f39a'><row id='.721' rev='1' h='5028204f'><cell id='.722' h='3615de84' header='true'><paragraph id='.723' h='68a8669e'><text id='.724'>Objection</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.733' h='9d230073' header='true'><paragraph id='.734' h='b2a3aa60'><text id='.735'>Answer</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.741' h='74b6a0e0' header='true'><paragraph id='.742' h='03867aea'><text id='.743'>Evidence</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.751' rev='3' h='c2050f1a'><cell id='.752' rev='1' h='e002079f'><paragraph id='.753' h='d6cd3521'><text id='.754'>The team already writes JavaScript</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.788' rev='3' h='5deca36d'><paragraph id='.789' h='c6cc271e'><text id='.790'>Familiarity favo</text><text id='.1735'>u</text><text id='.806'>rs Node.js for that team; the thesis assumes the repository's existing runtime is Python</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.894' rev='1' h='096de61d'><paragraph id='.895' h='fb1e38c2'><text id='.896'>Author's judgment</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.913' h='c677e51c'><cell id='.914' h='b0ddf823'><paragraph id='.915' h='ff47362e'><text id='.916'>Distribution of a single script may differ</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.958' h='036b490c'><paragraph id='.959' h='6402b8cc'><text id='.960'>The assessment has no finding on distribution; the thesis does not rely on it</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1037' h='b8067ba1'><paragraph id='.1038' h='f24bd1c6'><text id='.1039'>TA-001, Contradictions and Gaps</text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.1070' h='0738ee00' heading='2'><text id='.1071'>Recommendations</text></paragraph><table id='.1086' h='0e892b12'><row id='.1087' h='cf53a4ec'><cell id='.1088' h='bf688f94' header='true'><paragraph id='.1089' h='3169ce64'><text id='.1090'>Technology</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1100' h='208f5c01' header='true'><paragraph id='.1101' h='f30eedd9'><text id='.1102'>Stance</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1108' h='d2e0d8de' header='true'><paragraph id='.1109' h='a6e600a1'><text id='.1110'>Context</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1117' h='b8281590' header='true'><paragraph id='.1118' h='97d4be89'><text id='.1119'>Conditions</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1129' h='72303772' header='true'><paragraph id='.1130' h='e90a7726'><text id='.1131'>Based on</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1139' h='6a2e4089'><cell id='.1140' h='51982567'><paragraph id='.1141' h='18885f27'><text id='.1142'>Python</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1148' h='bfcce6b9'><paragraph id='.1149' h='107225fd'><text id='.1150'>Use with conditions (Proposed)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1180' h='9de980a8'><paragraph id='.1181' h='1eeceea6'><text id='.1182'>repository-tooling</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1200' h='1fd7f6ca'><paragraph id='.1201' h='5971adf4'><text id='.1202'>The repository already uses Python and no script needs a Node.js-only library.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1280' h='0fc729c9'><paragraph id='.1281' h='03c7f763'><text id='.1282'>TA-001</text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.1288' h='b5d828fa' heading='2'><text id='.1289'>Limits of the Position</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.1311' h='e4196365'><text id='.1312'>The paper does not claim Python is better in general. It fails where the repository's existing runtime is Node.js, or a required library exists only for Node.js.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.1473' h='03867aea' heading='2'><text id='.1474'>Evidence</text></paragraph><table id='.1482' h='5560cd98'><row id='.1483' h='43d99904'><cell id='.1484' h='c71a950d' header='true'><paragraph id='.1485' h='71bf9093'><text id='.1486'>Reference</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1495' h='77a586f6' header='true'><paragraph id='.1496' h='f5387f9b'><text id='.1497'>Kind</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1501' h='17da6e88' header='true'><paragraph id='.1502' h='2e516d68'><text id='.1503'>Revision</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1511' h='911374aa' header='true'><paragraph id='.1512' h='9cd881a5'><text id='.1513'>Used for</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1521' h='31502b57'><cell id='.1522' h='ec84740b'><paragraph id='.1523' h='03c7f763'><text id='.1524'>TA-001</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1530' h='1fdb7e66'><paragraph id='.1531' h='cb4787fa'><text id='.1532'>Technology assessment</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1553' h='6288d80e'><paragraph id='.1554' h='50d858e0'><text id='.1555'>example</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1562' h='3ef1c738'><paragraph id='.1563' h='746358eb'><text id='.1564'>Argument step 1</text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.1579' h='8a7525b1' heading='2'><text id='.1580'>Notes</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.1585' h='a1933b7e'><text id='.1586'>Configure </text><text id='.1596'><code>app.yaml</code></text><text id='.1604'> and see </text><text id='.1613'><link href='https://example.com/guide'>the guide</link></text><text id='.1622'> and [[tech-spike]] for pg_cron setup.</text></paragraph><list id='.1660' h='254fe926' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.1661' h='e886c8d5'><paragraph id='.1662' h='3b9be700'><text id='.1663'>Outer item one</text></paragraph><list id='.1677' h='06cc2e9c' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.1678' h='dd74a612'><paragraph id='.1679' h='96e5eb7c'><text id='.1680'>Nested item a</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.1693' h='bd7fdf27'><paragraph id='.1694' h='5b519551'><text id='.1695'>Nested item b</text></paragraph></listItem></list></listItem><listItem id='.1708' h='129f4f7c'><paragraph id='.1709' h='79b0f0f6'><text id='.1710'>Outer item two</text></paragraph></listItem></list></doc>
